94139534914 true] [17592186319421 1100 "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\\,i+xy\\,j$ at the indicated points?" 13194139534914 true] [17592186319421 1113 #uuid "a6e4754b-623a-592f-86c3-7bca425b2a5a" 13194139534914 true] [17592186319421 1145 "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),(1,2),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\\,i+xy\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-1,1) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(-1)(1)\\,j=-3\\,i-j \\\\ F(1,2) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(1)(2)\\,j=3\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,-1) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\,i+(2)(-1)\\,j=-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png)" 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319423 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319424 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319425 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319426 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186319427 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1041 "selection" 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1104 #edb/ref 17592186319423 13194139534914 true] [17592186319422 1110 #uuid "ea079116-6174-5adf-86ff-c05e14ec3885" 13194139534914 true] [17592186319423 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043096/assets/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644